<DocsLayout title="Getting Started with Aurora" description="A practical orientation guide for users and contributors exploring Aurora." heading="Getting started" eyebrow="DOCUMENTATION / FIRST STEPS">
<p class="docs-kicker">START HERE</p>
<h2>First, choose what you want to do.</h2>
<p>Aurora is an independent computing ecosystem with two primary product workstreams: Aurora OS and Lumen, the Aurora Browser. This website is the public place to understand the projects, follow verified progress and find documentation.</p>
<div class="docs-audience-grid docs-audience-grid-compact">
  <article class="docs-audience-card">
    <p class="docs-kicker">I WANT TO USE AURORA</p>
    <h3>Explore the products.</h3>
    <p>Read the <a href="/en/ecosystem/os/">Aurora OS overview</a> or the <a href="/en/ecosystem/browser/">Lumen overview</a>, then check <a href="/en/development/">current status</a> and <a href="/en/downloads/">verified downloads</a>.</p>
    <p class="docs-inline-status">No verified public installation release is currently listed.</p>
  </article>
  <article class="docs-audience-card">
    <p class="docs-kicker">I WANT TO CONTRIBUTE</p>
    <h3>Start with the code and evidence.</h3>
    <p>Read the <a href="/en/docs/developer-guide/">developer guide</a>, review the <a href="/en/engineering/architecture/">architecture</a> and follow the <a href="/en/community/contributing/">contribution workflow</a>.</p>
    <p class="docs-inline-status">The website repository is public. The Aurora OS repository is private.</p>
  </article>
</div>
<h2>Understand project status</h2>
<p>Do not assume that a described feature is ready to use. The <a href="/en/development/">development pages</a> distinguish implementation, testing, integration and planned work. A passing website build does not verify Aurora OS or Lumen.</p>
<div class="docs-callout"><strong>Before installing</strong><p>Only use release files linked from the <a href="/en/downloads/">downloads page</a>. If no verified artifact and matching instructions are listed, there is no supported public installation path yet.</p></div>
</DocsLayout>
